    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Why does AI forget what I said earlier?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "chat",
          "label": "EARLY CHAT"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "brain",
          "label": "FORGOTTEN?"
        },
        "mid": "VS",
        "subtitle": "Context windows, explained"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Because it can only look at a limited amount of text at once. That's called the context window.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "eye",
        "text": "Context window = what it can see",
        "cue": "window"
      },
      "punch": "window"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Like a short memory?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Kind of. Imagine reading a long book through a small window. Old pages slide out of view.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "THE WINDOW",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Reads through a window",
            "icon": "eye",
            "cue": "reading"
          },
          {
            "label": "New text comes in",
            "icon": "doc",
            "cue": "long"
          },
          {
            "label": "Old pages slide out",
            "icon": "x",
            "cue": "slide"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Doesn't it remember me between chats?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Some apps have a memory feature you can turn on or off. Otherwise, each new chat starts fresh.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "NEW CHAT",
          "color": "#0A84FF",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Usually starts fresh",
              "icon": "doc",
              "cue": "fresh"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "MEMORY ON",
          "color": "#E91E63",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Remembers some facts",
              "icon": "brain",
              "cue": "memory"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So how do I stop it forgetting?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Put the important details in one message. Or start a new chat with a short summary.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "FIXES",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Key details in one message",
            "icon": "doc",
            "cue": "important"
          },
          {
            "label": "Start a new chat",
            "icon": "chat",
            "cue": "start"
          },
          {
            "label": "Paste a short summary",
            "icon": "check",
            "cue": "summary"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#2ECC71"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Can I ask it to summarize first?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Yes! Ask it to summarize the chat so far, then paste that summary into a fresh chat.",
      "board": {
        "type": "chat",
        "title": "SMART TRICK",
        "items": [
          {
            "who": "user",
            "text": "Summarize our chat so far",
            "cue": "summarize"
          },
          {
            "who": "user",
            "text": "Paste into a new chat",
            "cue": "paste"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#0A84FF"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So: it sees a window, not everything.",
